cgroups.json for the Waydroid container on kugo (LineageOS 17.1 image's file, two entries removed).

Kernel 4.4 has no cgroup namespaces, so Android's init in the container mounts the host's real
cgroup hierarchies. The original file then made the host's memory hierarchy root 0700
(root:system), and init.rc chmods the cgroup2 mount (/dev/cg2_bpf, the host's unified hierarchy)
to 0600. The Sailfish user session (uid 100000) could no longer create or enter cgroups: every
user service failed with status=219/CGROUP, and lipstick could not be restarted.

Removed: the "memory" controller (memcg is only used for per-app memory limits, off by default)
and "Cgroups2" (eBPF network accounting). cpu, cpuacct, cpuset, blkio and schedtune stay.
